      "title": "Corpus — committing an accepted edit",
      "description": "The contract the `corpus` role is held to when an accepted edit is committed into it: take the write only on the editor's acceptance, as one change with its QA sidecars, under the commit-hygiene requirement and with no relaxing of that policy. The narrowest contract the editing diagram requires. A mechanical role's skill is a contract to test against, not instructions to read.",
